<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">USS Cole bombing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2000">2000</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The USS Cole bombing was a suicide attack by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> on the American destroyer USS Cole while it was refuelling in the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, on 12 October 2000. Two men steered a small boat packed with explosives against the ship's hull, killing 17 American sailors and wounding dozens. It was one of the deadliest attacks on a US warship since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uss-cole-bombing.jpg" alt="USS Cole bombing" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DoD photo by Sgt. Don L. Maes, U.S. Marine Corps. (Released) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Cole_(DDG-67)_Departs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
